ason so the orchestrator can act.\n','\n', char(10)), 'reviewer', 'done', 86, 'user', 1779697754, NULL, 1779763031, 'dir', '/home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Audit trace satisfied: sibling reviewer t_66e61c98 (no-parent runnable) executed the actual READ-ONLY review of producer per blocked-producer-reviewer pattern. Conclusion mirrored here. See t_66e61c98 for full evidence.', 'ssh-mcp-review-impl-audit-log', 0, NULL, NULL, 2700, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'tasks'(_rowid_, 'id', 'title', 'body', 'assignee', 'status', 'priority', 'created_by', 'created_at', 'started_at', 'completed_at', 'workspace_kind', 'workspace_path', 'branch_name', 'claim_lock', 'claim_expires', 'tenant', 'result', 'idempotency_key', 'consecutive_failures', 'worker_pid', 'last_failure_error', 'max_runtime_seconds', 'last_heartbeat_at', 'current_run_id', 'workflow_template_id', 'current_step_key', 'skills', 'model_override', 'max_retries', 'session_id') VALUES (17, 't_2366a62d', 'REVIEW: approval (t_c857745f)', replace('Acceptance review for the implementation card t_c857745f (approval).\n\nTrigger: this card will become claimable when the implementation worker calls kanban_block(reason=''review-required: ...''). Read parent task result, comments (look for changed_files / tests_run / diff_path), and worktree path; do not modify code.\n\nPass criteria specific to approval:\n- yolo allow only after audit log still records the decision.\n- smart: structured JSON {allow, reason}; timeout/non-200/malformed -> fail_closed deny by default.\n- smart: fetch wrapper is stubbable in tests; API key sourced from env reference not plaintext.\n- manual: pending records keyed by stable id, lifecycle pending/approved/denied/timeout, default 5-min timeout.\n- manual mode without WebUI must hard-fail at boot.\n- Engine wired BEFORE transport.exec; deny throws McpError with reason; allow proceeds and emits approval block into audit record.\n\nGeneral security criteria for every impl card:\n- No secret leakage in logs, status, or test snapshots.\n- TOML schema does not require plaintext credentials; env reference path is testable.\n- Tests use mocks/fakes; no destructive remote commands.\n- Existing legacy behavior preserved unless plan explicitly overrides.\n\nOn PASS:\n- Unblock the impl card (kanban_unblock).\n- Drop a comment naming verification evidence and any caveats.\n\nOn FAIL/YELLOW/RED:\n- Keep impl card blocked.\n- Drop a comment naming exact defects and required fixes.\n- Block this review card with a clear reason so the orchestrator can act.\n','\n', char(10)), 'reviewer', 'done', 86, 'user', 1779697755, NULL, 1779763031, 'dir', '/home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Audit trace satisfied: sibling reviewer t_a2698fcc (no-parent runnable) executed the actual READ-ONLY review of producer per blocked-producer-reviewer pattern. Conclusion mirrored here. See t_a2698fcc for full evidence.', 'ssh-mcp-review-impl-approval', 0, NULL, NULL, 2700, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'tasks'(_rowid_, 'id', 'title', 'body', 'assignee', 'status', 'priority', 'created_by', 'created_at', 'started_at', 'completed_at', 'workspace_kind', 'workspace_path', 'branch_name', 'claim_lock', 'claim_expires', 'tenant', 'result', 'idempotency_key', 'consecutive_failures', 'worker_pid', 'last_failure_error', 'max_runtime_seconds', 'last_heartbeat_at', 'current_run_id', 'workflow_template_id', 'current_step_key', 'skills', 'model_override', 'max_retries', 'session_id') VALUES (18, 't_fa50ed7d', 'REVIEW: webui-status (t_4e2a635b)', replace('Acceptance review for the implementation card t_4e2a635b (webui-status).\n\nTrigger: this card will become claimable when the implementation worker calls kanban_block(reason=''review-required: ...''). Read parent task result, comments (look for changed_files / tests_run / diff_path), and worktree path; do not modify code.\n\nPass criteria specific to webui-status:\n- Off by default; opt-in via TOML or --webui.\n- Default 127.0.0.1; non-loopback bind requires auth_token at boot or fatal.\n- Bearer token check on /api/* and ?token= for SSE.\n- Routes match plan: profiles, executions (limit cap), approvals (GET + POST allow/deny), /events SSE.\n- Manual approval round-trip verified by integration test.\n- No credential-like data leaked in any response or static asset.\n\nGeneral security criteria for every impl card:\n- No secret leakage in logs, status, or test snapshots.\n- TOML schema does not require plaintext credentials; env reference path is testable.\n- Tests use mocks/fakes; no destructive remote commands.\n- Existing legacy behavior preserved unless plan explicitly overrides.\n\nOn PASS:\n- Unblock the impl card (kanban_unblock).\n- Drop a comment naming verification evidence and any caveats.\n\nOn FAIL/YELLOW/RED:\n- Keep impl card blocked.\n- Drop a comment naming exact defects and required fixes.\n- Block this review card with a clear reason so the orchestrator can act.\n','\n', char(10)), 'reviewer', 'done', 86, 'user', 1779697755, NULL, 1779763032, 'dir', '/home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Audit trace satisfied: sibling reviewer t_b6b0762e (no-parent runnable) executed the actual READ-ONLY review of producer per blocked-producer-reviewer pattern. Conclusion mirrored here. See t_b6b0762e for full evidence.', 'ssh-mcp-review-impl-webui-status', 0, NULL, NULL, 2700, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'tasks'(_rowid_, 'id', 'title', 'body', 'assignee', 'status', 'priority', 'created_by', 'created_at', 'started_at', 'completed_at', 'workspace_kind', 'workspace_path', 'branch_name', 'claim_lock', 'claim_expires', 'tenant', 'result', 'idempotency_key', 'consecutive_failures', 'worker_pid', 'last_failure_error', 'max_runtime_seconds', 'last_heartbeat_at', 'current_run_id', 'workflow_template_id', 'current_step_key', 'skills', 'model_override', 'max_retries', 'session_id') VALUES (19, 't_a0d392f1', 'S1: consolidated security audit before e2e', replace('Consolidated security audit across TOML config, audit logging, approval engine, and WebUI status.\n\nInputs: all four per-impl REVIEW cards (must be PASS), implementation worktrees, plan at .hermes/plans/2026-05-25_ssh-mcp-toml-audit-approvals-webui.md.\n\nHard gates (ALL must hold):\n- Smart approval fail-closed verified by tests: timeout, non-200, malformed JSON, missing api key.\n- API keys never required in plaintext TOML; env reference path covered by tests.\n- No secret leakage across logs, status responses, SSE events, static WebUI assets, or test fixtures.\n- WebUI bind defaults loopback; non-loopback requires auth_token; SSE requires token; bearer enforced on /api.\n- Approval engine wired BEFORE transport.exec so denials cannot reach remote host.\n- Manual approval pending ids are stable, lifecycle is enforced, timeout default applied; manual mode without WebUI hard-fails at boot.\n- Audit log redaction handles password/PEM/JWT/AWS shapes; stdout/stderr bounded; rotation/retention honored.\n- Tests use mocks/fakes/local containers; no destructive remote commands.\n\nOn PASS: comment with verification evidence and unblock dependent e2e card (t_5d02508b) via kanban_unblock if it is blocked, otherwise just PASS.\nOn FAIL: block this card with a clear reason and a per-impl remediation list. Orchestrator will report to user.\n','\n', char(10)), 'reviewer', 'todo', 78, 'user', 1779697756, NULL, NULL, 'dir', '/home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ssh-mcp-s1-security-audit-before-e2e', 0, NULL, NULL, 3600, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'tasks'(_rowid_, 'id', 'title', 'body', 'assignee', 'status', 'priority', 'created_by', 'created_at', 'started_at', 'completed_at', 'workspace_kind', 'workspace_path', 'branch_name', 'claim_lock', 'claim_expires', 'tenant', 'result', 'idempotency_key', 'consecutive_failures', 'worker_pid', 'last_failure_error', 'max_runtime_seconds', 'last_heartbeat_at', 'current_run_id', 'workflow_template_id', 'current_step_key', 'skills', 'model_override', 'max_retries', 'session_id') VALUES (20, 't_a3c8b5e1', 'R1: HTTP MCP transport + Windows Kerberos deployment research', replace('Purpose: deployment-scenario research for Windows-host ssh-mcp + WSL Hermes Agent.\n\nContext (authoritative deployment fact from user):\n- ssh-mcp must run on the Windows host because it needs to use the Windows Kerberos credential (SSPI) for GSSAPI auth.\n- WSL-side Hermes Agent must invoke ssh-mcp tools over HTTP (Streamable HTTP MCP transport).\n- WSL2 mirrored networking is active in user''s environment: 127.0.0.1 loopback is unified between Windows host and WSL distro.\n\nDo NOT modify any code. Research only.\n\nRequired findings:\n1. Current ssh-mcp index.ts startup: confirm it is stdio-only and identify the smallest patchable surface to add an HTTP transport entrypoint without breaking stdio mode.\n2. @modelcontextprotocol/sdk version pinned in package.json: does it expose StreamableHTTPServerTransport (or its current equivalent)? Cite SDK version + exact import path.\n3. Recommended HTTP mount path, DNS rebinding guard, CORS/Origin handling, auth (bearer token vs mTLS) for an MCP server reachable from another machine/OS.\n4. Kerberos / GSSAPI feasibility in current ssh2 npm dep on Windows: does ssh2 use SSPI on Windows Node, or does it require Cygwin/MIT Kerberos? Cite ssh2 issues/docs.\n5. Node-on-Windows Kerberos quirks: SPN format, ticket cache, delegation, fallback to password/key when no ticket.\n6. Interaction with approval engine: smart-mode LLM endpoint must be reachable from Windows host (corporate proxy considerations). Recommend env var convention.\n7. Risks: secret leakage through HTTP body/headers in audit log; loopback-mirroring + WebUI binding implications; multi-instance race (Windows host vs WSL accidentally both running ssh-mcp).\n8. Recommended deployment topology and an autostart pattern for ssh-mcp on Windows (service / Task Scheduler / Startup).\n\nDeliverable in task result:\n- Concrete file paths + line refs.\n- SDK API names + minimal startup snippet (research-only, do not edit).\n- Risk/unknown list labelled GREEN/YELLOW/RED.\n','\n', char(10)), 'researcher', 'done', 92, 'user', 1779761634, 1779761669, 1779761884, 'dir', '/home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ssh-mcp-r1-http-transport-windows-kerberos', 0, NULL, NULL, 2700, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'tasks'(_rowid_, 'id', 'title', 'body', 'assignee', 'status', 'priority', 'created_by', 'created_at', 'started_at', 'completed_at', 'workspace_kind', 'workspace_path', 'branch_name', 'claim_lock', 'claim_expires', 'tenant', 'result', 'idempotency_key', 'consecutive_failures', 'worker_pid', 'last_failure_error', 'max_runtime_seconds', 'last_heartbeat_at', 'current_run_id', 'workflow_template_id', 'current_step_key', 'skills', 'model_override', 'max_retries', 'session_id') VALUES (21, 't_00777089', 'P2: design HTTP MCP transport + Windows Kerberos integration', replace('Purpose: design the HTTP/Streamable-HTTP MCP transport addition and the Windows-host Kerberos deployment surface, consuming R1.\n\nConstraints:\n- Do not break stdio MCP transport. Default behavior must remain stdio when neither --http nor [server.http] in TOML is set.\n- Add opt-in HTTP transport via TOML [server.http] block AND/OR --http CLI flag (mutually compatible with --config + --ssh + legacy).\n- Bind default: 127.0.0.1 on a fixed port (recommend 7022 or whatever R1 finds free). Non-loopback bind MUST require an auth token at boot or fatal.\n- Bearer token + Origin allowlist + DNS-rebinding guard required (per MCP spec for Streamable HTTP).\n- Honor existing approval/audit/webui security posture: smart fail-closed, secret redaction, bounded stdout/stderr.\n- Kerberos: ssh2 transport must work on Windows Node using SSPI; if R1 says ssh2 cannot do SSPI directly, design a fallback that calls Windows klist/kinit or uses an alternative SSH lib, with explicit YELLOW handoff.\n- Windows host autostart guidance (Task Scheduler / nssm / Service Wrapper) belongs in docs, not in code.\n\nDeliverables:\n- Implementation plan covering files/modules to add/change.\n- TOML schema delta:\n  [server.http]\n  enabled = false\n  bind = "127.0.0.1"\n  port = 7022\n  auth_token_env = "SSH_MCP_HTTP_TOKEN"\n  origin_allowlist = ["http://localhost", "http://127.0.0.1"]\n  request_timeout_ms = 60000\n- Acceptance criteria mirroring stdio behaviour parity.\n- Test matrix: stdio still works; HTTP boots; bearer enforced; rebinding rejected; missing token on non-loopback fatal; Kerberos auth path on Windows verified (mock-friendly).\n- Explicit GREEN/YELLOW/RED list; RED items block dev.\n','\n', char(10)), 'planner', 'done', 90, 'user', 1779761635, 1779761910, 1779762098, 'dir', '/home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ssh-mcp-p2-design-http-transport-windows', 0, NULL, NULL, 2700, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'tasks'(_rowid_, 'id', 'title', 'body', 'assignee', 'status', 'priority', 'created_by', 'created_at', 'started_at', 'completed_at', 'workspace_kind', 'workspace_path', 'branch_name', 'claim_lock', 'claim_expires', 'tenant', 'result', 'idempotency_key', 'consecutive_failures', 'worker_pid', 'last_failure_error', 'max_runtime_seconds', 'last_heartbeat_at', 'current_run_id', 'workflow_template_id', 'current_step_key', 'skills', 'model_override', 'max_retries', 'session_id') VALUES (22, 't_a60efb40', 'ssh-mcp: HTTP MCP transport + Windows Kerberos compatibility', replace('Implement Streamable HTTP MCP transport for ssh-mcp-kerberos plus Windows-host Kerberos compatibility per P2 design.\n\nWorkspace constraint: isolated worktree only; do not touch other worktrees.\n\nScope:\n1. Add HTTP transport startup path next to existing stdio. Default OFF.\n2. TOML [server.http] block (enabled/bind/port/auth_token_env/origin_allowlist/request_timeout_ms) wired through toml-config loader (parent t_2d87e8fa). If schema mismatch, propose smallest delta and add tests.\n3. Bearer auth + Origin allowlist + DNS-rebinding guard per MCP Streamable HTTP spec.\n4. Non-loopback bind without auth token MUST fatal at boot.\n5. Audit log: include transport=stdio|http and remote_addr (only when non-loopback) in records; never log bearer token.\n6. Approval engine and WebUI status surface continue to work when transport is HTTP.\n7. Windows Kerberos: ensure ssh2 transport uses SSPI on Windows; if ssh2 limitation, document fallback (Pageant/kinit/file-based ticket) with TODO and test stub.\n8. Tests:\n   - HTTP transport handshake (initialize -> list tools -> call exec stub) over HTTP.\n   - Bearer enforced; missing token rejected.\n   - Non-loopback + missing token = fatal at boot.\n   - Origin allowlist enforced.\n   - stdio mode still passes existing suite (no regressions).\n   - Audit record contains transport/remote_addr correctly.\n9. Docs delta will be handled later by docs card; just leave a README stub note.\n\nCompletion result must include:\n- Branch/worktree path + commit SHAs.\n- Files changed, npm test summary.\n- Any Windows-Kerberos issue labelled YELLOW with concrete repro path so reviewer/user can decide.\n\nEnd with kanban_block(reason="review-required: http mcp transport + windows kerberos") after handoff comment.\n','\n', char(10)), 'developer-general', 'archived', 82, 'user', 1779761635, 1779762150, NULL, 'worktree', '/home/islaliu/.hermes/hermes-agent/.worktrees/t_a60efb40', 'feat/ssh-mcp-http-transport', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ssh-mcp-dev-http-transport-windows-kerberos', 0, NULL, NULL, 10800, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'tasks'(_rowid_, 'id', 'title', 'body', 'assignee', 'status', 'priority', 'created_by', 'created_at', 'started_at', 'completed_at', 'workspace_kind', 'workspace_path', 'branch_name', 'claim_lock', 'claim_expires', 'tenant', 'result', 'idempotency_key', 'consecutive_failures', 'worker_pid', 'last_failure_error', 'max_runtime_seconds', 'last_heartbeat_at', 'current_run_id', 'workflow_template_id', 'current_step_key', 'skills', 'model_override', 'max_retries', 'session_id') VALUES (23, 't_b149430f', 'REVIEW: http-transport + windows kerberos', replace('Acceptance review for HTTP MCP transport + Windows Kerberos card.\n\nTrigger: parent will become blocked with reason starting ''review-required:''.\n\nPass criteria:\n- stdio transport behaviour preserved with no regressions.\n- HTTP transport boots only when opt-in TOML/flag is set.\n- Bearer token required for non-loopback; missing token = fatal at boot.\n- Origin allowlist + DNS-rebinding guard enforced; tests demonstrate rejected requests.\n- No secret/bearer/token logged in audit, status, or stderr.\n- Audit record carries transport and remote_addr fields correctly (loopback omitted/empty).\n- Windows SSPI/Kerberos path documented; YELLOW gaps clearly listed with repro.\n- Approval engine still gates exec before transport, regardless of transport type.\n\nOn PASS: unblock parent and drop verification evidence comment.\nOn FAIL/YELLOW/RED: keep blocked with exact remediation list; block this review card with reason ''blocker for user''.\n','\n', char(10)), 'reviewer', 'archived', 84, 'user', 1779761636, NULL, NULL, 'dir', '/home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ssh-mcp-review-http-transport', 0, NULL, NULL, 2700, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'tasks'(_rowid_, 'id', 'title', 'body', 'assignee', 'status', 'priority', 'created_by', 'created_at', 'started_at', 'completed_at', 'workspace_kind', 'workspace_path', 'branch_name', 'claim_lock', 'claim_expires', 'tenant', 'result', 'idempotency_key', 'consecutive_failures', 'worker_pid', 'last_failure_error', 'max_runtime_seconds', 'last_heartbeat_at', 'current_run_id', 'workflow_template_id', 'current_step_key', 'skills', 'model_override', 'max_retries', 'session_id') VALUES (24, 't_58c0e613', 'ssh-mcp: Windows-host HTTP MCP smoke runbook', replace('Produce a Windows-host smoke runbook (Markdown + .ps1) for ssh-mcp HTTP MCP transport.\n\nCannot execute on Windows from this WSL agent; deliver a runbook that the user can run on the Windows host.\n\nRunbook must:\n- Resolve ssh-mcp Windows install path or recommend npm i -g / pnpm dlx invocation.\n- Start ssh-mcp with [server.http] enabled and a sample TOML at %USERPROFILE%\.ssh-mcp\config.toml.\n- Verify Kerberos ticket via klist; if missing, kinit (or domain login) instructions.\n- POST initialize/list_tools/call_tool exec against http://127.0.0.1:<port>/mcp with bearer.\n- From WSL side: curl the same endpoint to confirm mirrored networking reachability.\n- Tear down (Ctrl+C) and verify audit log entries at %USERPROFILE%\.ssh-mcp\logs.\n\nDeliverable:\n- Saved at .hermes/runbooks/windows-smoke-http-mcp.md (and optional companion .ps1 next to it).\n- Include success criteria the user can tick.\n- Mark dependencies / prerequisites / known caveats.\n','\n', char(10)), 'documenter', 'done', 76, 'user', 1779761637, 1779762922, 1779763406, 'dir', '/home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ssh-mcp-windows-host-smoke-runbook', 0, NULL, NULL, 2700, 1779763073, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'tasks'(_rowid_, 'id', 'title', 'body', 'assignee', 'status', 'priority', 'created_by', 'created_at', 'started_at', 'completed_at', 'workspace_kind', 'workspace_path', 'branch_name', 'claim_lock', 'claim_expires', 'tenant', 'result', 'idempotency_key', 'consecutive_failures', 'worker_pid', 'last_failure_error', 'max_runtime_seconds', 'last_heartbeat_at', 'current_run_id', 'workflow_template_id', 'current_step_key', 'skills', 'model_override', 'max_retries', 'session_id') VALUES (25, 't_b253463f', 'ssh-mcp: Windows service registration .bat (deployment option b)', replace('Produce a Windows service registration .bat helper for ssh-mcp on Windows host, plus a companion uninstall .bat.\n\nCannot execute on Windows from this WSL agent. Deliver the artifacts under .hermes/runbooks/ in this repo so user can copy to Windows side.\n\nDeliverables:\n1. register-ssh-mcp-service.bat\n   - Prefer nssm or sc.exe; recommend nssm because it gracefully handles npm/node child processes and restarts.\n   - Service name: ssh-mcp-kerberos.\n   - Working dir: McpsLaunch parent dir.\n   - Command: cmd /c StandaloneMcpServer.bat (so the existing launcher remains single source of truth).\n   - Account: LocalSystem cannot use the user''s Kerberos ticket. Service MUST run under the user''s domain account (or NetworkService with constrained delegation, document the trade-off). Document why and how to set account in the .bat or as a post-install step.\n   - Startup type: Automatic-Delayed-Start.\n   - Restart on failure (3 attempts, 30s delay).\n2. unregister-ssh-mcp-service.bat\n   - Idempotent uninstall: stop service, delete, no error if missing.\n3. README section under .hermes/runbooks/windows-service.md explaining:\n   - Why LocalSystem is wrong for Kerberos (no user ticket).\n   - How to grant the domain account ''Log on as a service'' right.\n   - Troubleshooting: klist as service account, Event Viewer hints.\n   - Coexistence with Task Scheduler (a) — choose one, not both, to avoid two instances.\n\nEnd with kanban_complete (docs only, no code review required).\n','\n', char(10)), 'documenter', 'archived', 74, 'user', 1779761924, NULL, NULL, 'dir', '/home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ssh-mcp-windows-service-register-bat', 0, NULL, NULL, 2700, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'tasks'(_rowid_, 'id', 'title', 'body', 'assignee', 'status', 'priority', 'created_by', 'created_at', 'started_at', 'completed_at', 'workspace_kind', 'workspace_path', 'branch_name', 'claim_lock', 'claim_expires', 'tenant', 'result', 'idempotency_key', 'consecutive_failures', 'worker_pid', 'last_failure_error', 'max_runtime_seconds', 'last_heartbeat_at', 'current_run_id', 'workflow_template_id', 'current_step_key', 'skills', 'model_override', 'max_retries', 'session_id') VALUES (26, 't_80035a6b', 'ssh-mcp: migration guide for StandaloneMcpServers.ps1 → TOML', replace('Produce a migration guide so the user can move /home/islaliu/Repositories/McpsLaunch/StandaloneMcpServers.ps1 onto the new ssh-mcp TOML/audit/approval/WebUI stack without breaking the current production launcher.\n\nDeliver as .hermes/runbooks/migrate-mcpslaunch-to-toml.md inside ssh-mcp-kerberos repo. DO NOT edit McpsLaunch — that is a different repo and user owns it.\n\nCover:\n1. Current state recap (port 8934, mcp-proxy bridge, --ssh=<JSON> for eip2-db + gitlab, Hyper-V firewall rule).\n2. Phase 1 (no behaviour change): drop a sample ssh-mcp.toml at %USERPROFILE%\.ssh-mcp\config.toml mirroring the two existing hosts; verify ssh-mcp --config=... yields identical tool listing.\n3. Phase 2: switch ps1 from inline --ssh=<JSON> to --config=%USERPROFILE%\.ssh-mcp\config.toml; keep mcp-proxy bridge.\n4. Phase 3 (only if P2 picks Option B): drop mcp-proxy wrapper, run ssh-mcp directly with [server.http] enabled, bind $WindowsMcpHost:8934, bearer via SSH_MCP_HTTP_TOKEN env var. Keep firewall rule unchanged because port number is the same.\n5. Phase 4: enable audit log + approval engine (start with approvals.mode = manual; switch to smart only after a soak period).\n6. Rollback for each phase (single edit reverts).\n7. Verification: from WSL `curl http://$WindowsMcpHost:8934/` (or equivalent) succeeds; from Windows browser the WebUI status page renders profiles and pending approvals.\n8. Known caveats: smart mode requires LLM endpoint reachable from Windows host; corporate proxy may need HTTPS_PROXY env var on the service.\n\nEnd with kanban_complete.\n','\n', char(10)), 'documenter', 'todo', 72, 'user', 1779761924, NULL, NULL, 'dir', '/home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ssh-mcp-migration-guide-mcpslaunch-to-toml', 0, NULL, NULL, 2700, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'tasks'(_rowid_, 'id', 'title', 'body', 'assignee', 'status', 'priority', 'created_by', 'created_at', 'started_at', 'completed_at', 'workspace_kind', 'workspace_path', 'branch_name', 'claim_lock', 'claim_expires', 'tenant', 'result', 'idempotency_key', 'consecutive_failures', 'worker_pid', 'last_failure_error', 'max_runtime_seconds', 'last_heartbeat_at', 'current_run_id', 'workflow_template_id', 'current_step_key', 'skills', 'model_override', 'max_retries', 'session_id') VALUES (27, 't_e33d1d5e', 'ssh-mcp: Windows Task Scheduler register .bat (deployment option a only)', replace('Produce Windows Task Scheduler registration helpers for ssh-mcp on Windows host (deployment option (a)). \n\nUSER DECISION (authoritative): option (b) Windows Service was rejected — Windows Service runs as LocalSystem/service account with its own LSA session and no domain Kerberos ticket, which breaks the kerberos-auth path that all production hosts use (R1 §8). Deliver Task Scheduler only.\n\nCannot execute on Windows from this WSL agent. Deliver artifacts under .hermes/runbooks/ in this repo so user can copy to Windows side.\n\nDeliverables:\n1. register-ssh-mcp-startup.bat\n   - Wraps `schtasks /Create /SC ONLOGON /RL HIGHEST /TN "ssh-mcp" /TR "<launcher>" /IT /F`.\n   - /IT flag REQUIRED so task runs in the interactive logon session (keeps LSA ticket for SSPI Kerberos).\n   - /RL HIGHEST so the task can bind privileged ports if user later moves off 8934.\n   - /F to overwrite any prior registration without prompt.\n   - Launcher target: by default the existing %~dp0..\McpsLaunch\StandaloneMcpServer.bat to preserve the current production launcher as single source of truth.\n   - Allow override via env var SSH_MCP_LAUNCHER if user moves the launcher elsewhere.\n   - Idempotent: schtasks /Query first; if exists, /Delete then /Create.\n   - Print a verification line at the end: schtasks /Query /TN ssh-mcp /V /FO LIST | findstr "Status"\n2. unregister-ssh-mcp-startup.bat\n   - schtasks /Delete /TN "ssh-mcp" /F; no error if task missing.\n3. README section .hermes/runbooks/windows-autostart.md\n   - Why Task Scheduler (interactive logon) — not Windows Service: LSA ticket lives per logon session, LocalSystem cannot use the user''s Kerberos ticket. Cite R1 §8 finding.\n   - How to verify: `klist` from cmd shows tickets; if empty after first logon, run `klist purge` then re-logon, or `cmdkey /add:* /user:DOMAIN\user /pass`.\n   - Coexistence rule: this Task Scheduler entry must be the ONLY ssh-mcp launcher on the host. Do NOT also start it from Startup folder or as a service — would create port-bind race (R1 risk RED).\n   - Troubleshooting: Event Viewer → Microsoft → Windows → TaskScheduler/Operational.\n   - If user later wants Windows Service for a non-Kerberos host: explicitly call out it would need a different ssh-mcp instance on a different port and would not handle the kerberos hosts.\n\nEnd with kanban_complete (docs only, no code review).\n','\n', char(10)), 'documenter', 'done', 74, 'user', 1779762074, 1779763463, 1779763894, 'dir', '/home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ssh-mcp-windows-task-scheduler-register-bat', 0, NULL, NULL, 2700, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
