INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (10, 't_c857745f', 'developer-general', replace('## Implementation handoff\n\n**Branch:** `feat/approval-engine` (worktree at `/home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos.wt/approval-engine`)\n**Commit:** `eb7bd7d806ae0cebcdd82a9f4e8e4f8589ff2887`\n**Diff:** `/tmp/approval-engine.diff` (1278 lines)\n\n### changed_files\n- `src/approval/types.ts` (new) — ApprovalMode/Decision/Context/Engine + self-contained ResolvedSource so we don''t block on toml-config\n- `src/approval/yolo.ts` (new)\n- `src/approval/smart.ts` (new) — OpenAI chat-completions schema, injectable fetch, fail-closed default\n- `src/approval/manual.ts` (new) — in-process ULID-keyed queue, external resolve, 5-min default timeout, fatal-at-boot when WebUI disabled\n- `src/approval/engine.ts` (new) — ApprovalDispatcher with per-source override\n- `src/approval/gate.ts` (new) — setApprovalEngine + gateApproval; legacy path = synthetic allow so existing tests untouched\n- `src/approval/index.ts` (new) — public barrel\n- `src/approval/__tests__/{engine,smart,manual,gate}.test.ts` (new)\n- `src/index.ts` — exec + sudo-exec handlers call `gateApproval` BEFORE `transport.exec`\n\n### tests_run\n- `npm test -- src/approval` → **35 passed / 0 failed** (4 files)\n- Full `npm test` → 81 passed / 29 failed (12 files); the 29 failures are pre-existing baseline failures requiring a live SSH testcontainer on `127.0.0.1:2222` and `localhost:22` (verified by running `git stash && npm test` on trunk → same 29 fail, 81 pass). **No new regressions introduced.**\n- `npm run build` (tsc + chmod) → clean.\n\n### Coverage map (DoD)\n- yolo allow → engine.test.ts + yolo via dispatcher\n- smart allow/deny/timeout/malformed JSON/non-200 under fail-closed AND fail-open → smart.test.ts (15 cases)\n- manual queue + external resolve + timeout + late-resolve no-op + multi-pending → manual.test.ts (8 cases)\n- exec gated allow/deny path → gate.test.ts (McpError on deny, allow passthrough, synthetic allow when engine unset)\n- manual-mode-without-WebUI throws at boot → manual.test.ts "boot guard"\n\n### Notes for reviewer\n- `ResolvedSource` is defined locally in `approval/types.ts`. Once toml-config (`t_2d87e8fa`) lands, reviewer should make `src/config/types.ts` re-export this or vice versa.\n- `ApprovalContext` carries the post-sanitize command and the raw description; audit-log card (`t_67320e65`) should stuff the returned `ApprovalDecision` verbatim into the `approval` block of each JSONL record.\n- `gate.ts` deny throws `McpError(InvalidRequest, "approval denied (<mode>/<decided_by>): <reason>")` — chosen over `InternalError` since it''s a policy rejection, not a server fault. Open to revision.\n- `manual.ts` uses a local 26-char Crockford-base32 id (no `ulid` dep) — keeps zero new runtime deps in this card. If we add `ulid` for audit-log, swap to the real lib.\n- WebUI-disabled-fatality is enforced at `ManualApproval` construction; boot wiring (TBD in webui-status card) must `new ManualApproval({webuiEnabled: <derived>})` so the error surfaces before MCP starts accepting traffic.','\n', char(10)), 1779698087);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (11, 't_4e2a635b', 'developer-general', replace('review-required handoff:\n\n```json\n{\n  "changed_files": [\n    "src/webui/server.ts",\n    "src/webui/types.ts",\n    "src/webui/routes/profiles.ts",\n    "src/webui/routes/executions.ts",\n    "src/webui/routes/approvals.ts",\n    "src/webui/routes/sse.ts",\n    "src/webui/static/index.html",\n    "src/webui/static/styles.css",\n    "src/webui/static/app.js",\n    "src/webui/__tests__/routes.test.ts"\n  ],\n  "tests_run": 13,\n  "tests_passed": 13,\n  "diff_path": "/home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos.wt/webui",\n  "branch": "wt/webui",\n  "commit": "e76f776",\n  "decisions": [\n    "Used node:http instead of express. Plan said ''Express + SSE'' but express isn''t in the existing package.json or node_modules; adding it and its types would pull ~30 transitive deps for what is effectively a 4-route server. node:http with manual routing keeps the surface in-tree, fully testable, and avoids a dep churn that the audit-log/approval-engine PRs would have to rebase across. Reviewer: flag if you''d prefer express anyway and I''ll switch.",\n    "Defined ManualApprovalQueue / AuditTail / RegistrySnapshot as TS interface stubs in src/webui/types.ts. Plan acknowledged this (Depends on approval-engine card ... let reviewer reconcile). Real types ship with t_c857745f (approval-engine) and t_67320e65 (audit-log).",\n    "Static UI gets the token from #token=... hash (stripped from URL bar on first read), localStorage, or the input box; no enforcement on the page itself because the user has nothing to authenticate with on first hit.",\n    "Auth: Bearer header (or X-Auth-Token fallback) on /api/*; ?token=<v> query for SSE /events (EventSource can''t set headers).",\n    "Non-loopback bind without authToken is a synchronous throw before listen() — boot-time fatal, per plan."\n  ],\n  "test_summary": {\n    "new_tests": "src/webui/__tests__/routes.test.ts — 13/13 passing",\n    "covers": [\n      "GET /api/profiles shape + approval mode",\n      "GET /api/executions limit + profile filter",\n      "GET /api/approvals listing",\n      "manual round-trip: enqueue -> GET shows -> POST allow -> decide promise resolves with allow + reason + decided_by",\n      "POST allow on unknown id -> 404",\n      "POST deny resolves promise with deny",\n      "static index served on loopback without token",\n      "non-loopback bind without authToken throws",\n      "loopback w/o token still allows (dev mode)",\n      "Bearer token required when authToken set",\n      "SSE /events 401 without token, 200 with ?token=",\n      "SSE broadcasts pending-approval on enqueue"\n    ],\n    "pre_existing_failures_not_regressions": [\n      "test/smoke.ssh.test.ts",\n      "test/description.test.ts",\n      "test/persistent-connection.test.ts",\n      "test/sudo-exec.test.ts"\n    ],\n    "pre_existing_failure_note": "All four require a live SSH server on 127.0.0.1:2222 (ECONNREFUSED). Confirmed identical failure pattern on base commit 7695120 with no webui changes — these are environment-dependent integration tests, not regressions."\n  },\n  "notes_for_e2e_card": [\n    "startWebUI(opts) returns { address: { host, port }, close() }. Pass port: 0 for an ephemeral port.",\n    "queue.on(''enqueue''|''resolve'') drives SSE pending-approval events; audit.on(''execution'') drives execution events.",\n    "When wiring into src/index.ts boot, gate behind opts.enabled || cliFlags.webui and pass the TransportRegistry as registry. getApprovalMode should be a thin wrapper over the resolved per-source approval mode from the toml-config card."\n  ]\n}\n```','\n', char(10)), 1779698260);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (12, 't_2d87e8fa', 'developer-general', replace('```json\n{\n  "changed_files": [\n    "package.json",\n    "package-lock.json",\n    "src/config/types.ts",\n    "src/config/toml-loader.ts",\n    "src/config/resolver.ts",\n    "src/config/__tests__/toml-loader.test.ts",\n    "src/config/__tests__/resolver.test.ts",\n    "src/index.ts",\n    "ssh-mcp.toml.example"\n  ],\n  "tests_run": [\n    { "command": "npm run build", "result": "pass" },\n    { "command": "npm test -- src/config/__tests__/toml-loader.test.ts src/config/__tests__/resolver.test.ts test/maxChars.test.ts test/openssh.unit.test.ts test/result-mapper.test.ts test/zod.compat.test.ts", "result": "pass", "tests": "69 passed" },\n    { "command": "npm test", "result": "fail", "reason": "Docker daemon/local SSH fixture unavailable: cannot connect to 127.0.0.1:2222; docker compose create failed with Cannot connect to Docker daemon" }\n  ],\n  "diff_path": "/home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos.wt/toml-config/.hermes/diffs/t_2d87e8fa-toml-config.diff",\n  "branch": "feat/toml-config",\n  "commit": "6e0df80",\n  "pr_url": "https://github.com/Isla-Liu/ssh-mcp/pull/1"\n}\n```','\n', char(10)), 1779699897);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (13, 't_67320e65', 'developer-general', replace('review-required handoff:\n```json\n{\n  "changed_files": [\n    "src/index.ts",\n    "tsconfig.json",\n    "src/audit/types.ts",\n    "src/audit/redactor.ts",\n    "src/audit/rotator.ts",\n    "src/audit/store.ts",\n    "src/audit/__tests__/redactor.test.ts",\n    "src/audit/__tests__/rotator.test.ts",\n    "src/audit/__tests__/store.test.ts",\n    "src/audit/__tests__/integration.test.ts"\n  ],\n  "tests_run": [\n    "rm -rf build && npm run build && npx vitest --run src/audit/__tests__ test/openssh.unit.test.ts (28/28 passed)",\n    "npm test (86/86 passed; used temporary lscr.io/linuxserver/openssh-server container on 127.0.0.1:2222, then removed it)"\n  ],\n  "diff_path": "/tmp/t_67320e65-audit-log.diff",\n  "decisions": [\n    "TOML audit_dir/audit_max_bytes wiring is left as TODO pending toml-config card; current implementation uses documented default ~/.ssh-mcp plus SSH_MCP_AUDIT_DIR/SSH_MCP_AUDIT_MAX_BYTES env overrides for tests/operators.",\n    "Approval section uses yolo placeholder until approval-engine card lands.",\n    "Audit append is best-effort after execution; an audit write failure is logged to stderr but does not mask the SSH tool result.",\n    "tsconfig excludes src/**/__tests__ from tsc build output so npm test does not double-run emitted build/audit tests after npm run build."\n  ]\n}\n```','\n', char(10)), 1779700700);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (14, 't_b94988d2', 'orchestrator', 'Deployment context (user, authoritative): ssh-mcp runs on Windows host to use Windows Kerberos credential (SSPI); WSL Hermes Agent invokes it over HTTP MCP transport. R0/P1 assumed stdio-only; added R1/P2/DEV/REVIEW/SMOKE cards to cover Streamable HTTP MCP transport, bearer/Origin/DNS-rebind guards, and Windows Kerberos path. WebUI status server (node:http) stays loopback default and remains reachable from WSL via mirrored networking.', 1779761639);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (15, 't_a0d392f1', 'orchestrator', 'S1 scope extended: also verify HTTP MCP transport hardening — bearer enforced, non-loopback bind requires token, Origin allowlist + DNS rebinding guard rejects spoofed Host headers, audit records carry transport/remote_addr without leaking bearer. Depends on DEV_HTTP t_a60efb40 + REVIEW_HTTP t_b149430f.', 1779761639);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (16, 't_5d02508b', 'orchestrator', 'E2E scope extended: smoke must exercise BOTH stdio and HTTP transports. HTTP transport test may use 127.0.0.1 inside the WSL test runner; Windows-host Kerberos verification is delivered as a separate runbook (t_58c0e613) that the user runs on Windows.', 1779761639);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (17, 't_a3c8b5e1', 'orchestrator', replace('GROUND TRUTH UPDATE from user — supersedes assumptions in R0/P1 about transport.\n\nssh-mcp-kerberos is ALREADY exposed via HTTP today, through an external bridge:\n- Launcher: /home/islaliu/Repositories/McpsLaunch/StandaloneMcpServers.ps1 (started by StandaloneMcpServer.bat)\n- Bridge: npx mcp-proxy --port=$SshMcpPort --host=$WindowsMcpHost -- node <ssh-mcp build/index.js> --ssh=<JSON> --ssh=<JSON>\n- ssh-mcp HTTP port: 8934\n- Bind: $WindowsMcpHost (single source of truth, Hyper-V vSwitch IP on Windows)\n- WSL subnet 192.168.144.0/24 already firewall-allowed via _Mcp Servers Allow Wsl only rule (Hyper-V firewall, ports 3000/8931/8932/8934/8935)\n- ssh-mcp parseArgv() only accepts --ssh=<JSON> (= form), not space form\n- Two production SSH hosts pinned in ps1 today: eip2-db and gitlab, both auth=kerberos\n\nUser constraints (authoritative):\n- Deployment topology = (a) Task Scheduler at logon running the existing .bat (preferred), optionally also (b) a Windows service registration .bat for convenience.\n- Tools registration is already HTTP via mcp-proxy; we are NOT starting from stdio-only.\n\nTrade-off the design must explicitly resolve (label GREEN/YELLOW/RED):\nOption A: KEEP mcp-proxy bridge unchanged; ssh-mcp itself remains stdio internally.\n  + Zero risk to current production launcher; smallest delta.\n  + ssh-mcp doesn''t take on Streamable HTTP SDK surface.\n  - bearer/Origin/DNS-rebind/audit-of-HTTP can only happen at mcp-proxy layer (or not at all). ssh-mcp can only see stdio frames and cannot record remote_addr or enforce token.\n  - Audit log will lack HTTP request metadata (caller IP, bearer presence, Origin) unless mcp-proxy provides it.\n  - Approval engine cannot bind allow/deny to a caller identity beyond stdio.\n\nOption B: Add Streamable HTTP MCP transport INSIDE ssh-mcp-kerberos; deprecate mcp-proxy in production path (keep stdio as fallback).\n  + bearer/Origin/DNS-rebind enforced inside ssh-mcp.\n  + Audit log can record transport, remote_addr, bearer-present, Origin per call.\n  + Approval engine can attach decision to caller identity and origin.\n  + One fewer process / less daemon plumbing in launcher.\n  - Touches index.ts startup more invasively; adds @modelcontextprotocol/sdk HTTP server surface dependency.\n  - Requires migration of StandaloneMcpServers.ps1 to drop the mcp-proxy wrapper.\n\nR1 must produce a decision recommendation with cited evidence. P2 then locks the choice.\n\nMigration constraint: --ssh=<JSON> form must remain valid even after TOML lands so the current ps1 keeps working until user migrates to --config.\n\nCross-repo touch: StandaloneMcpServers.ps1 lives in McpsLaunch, NOT in ssh-mcp-kerberos. Do not edit it from this board; documenter will produce a migration guide.','\n', char(10)), 1779761922);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (18, 't_00777089', 'orchestrator', replace('GROUND TRUTH UPDATE from user — supersedes assumptions in R0/P1 about transport.\n\nssh-mcp-kerberos is ALREADY exposed via HTTP today, through an external bridge:\n- Launcher: /home/islaliu/Repositories/McpsLaunch/StandaloneMcpServers.ps1 (started by StandaloneMcpServer.bat)\n- Bridge: npx mcp-proxy --port=$SshMcpPort --host=$WindowsMcpHost -- node <ssh-mcp build/index.js> --ssh=<JSON> --ssh=<JSON>\n- ssh-mcp HTTP port: 8934\n- Bind: $WindowsMcpHost (single source of truth, Hyper-V vSwitch IP on Windows)\n- WSL subnet 192.168.144.0/24 already firewall-allowed via _Mcp Servers Allow Wsl only rule (Hyper-V firewall, ports 3000/8931/8932/8934/8935)\n- ssh-mcp parseArgv() only accepts --ssh=<JSON> (= form), not space form\n- Two production SSH hosts pinned in ps1 today: eip2-db and gitlab, both auth=kerberos\n\nUser constraints (authoritative):\n- Deployment topology = (a) Task Scheduler at logon running the existing .bat (preferred), optionally also (b) a Windows service registration .bat for convenience.\n- Tools registration is already HTTP via mcp-proxy; we are NOT starting from stdio-only.\n\nTrade-off the design must explicitly resolve (label GREEN/YELLOW/RED):\nOption A: KEEP mcp-proxy bridge unchanged; ssh-mcp itself remains stdio internally.\n  + Zero risk to current production launcher; smallest delta.\n  + ssh-mcp doesn''t take on Streamable HTTP SDK surface.\n  - bearer/Origin/DNS-rebind/audit-of-HTTP can only happen at mcp-proxy layer (or not at all). ssh-mcp can only see stdio frames and cannot record remote_addr or enforce token.\n  - Audit log will lack HTTP request metadata (caller IP, bearer presence, Origin) unless mcp-proxy provides it.\n  - Approval engine cannot bind allow/deny to a caller identity beyond stdio.\n\nOption B: Add Streamable HTTP MCP transport INSIDE ssh-mcp-kerberos; deprecate mcp-proxy in production path (keep stdio as fallback).\n  + bearer/Origin/DNS-rebind enforced inside ssh-mcp.\n  + Audit log can record transport, remote_addr, bearer-present, Origin per call.\n  + Approval engine can attach decision to caller identity and origin.\n  + One fewer process / less daemon plumbing in launcher.\n  - Touches index.ts startup more invasively; adds @modelcontextprotocol/sdk HTTP server surface dependency.\n  - Requires migration of StandaloneMcpServers.ps1 to drop the mcp-proxy wrapper.\n\nR1 must produce a decision recommendation with cited evidence. P2 then locks the choice.\n\nMigration constraint: --ssh=<JSON> form must remain valid even after TOML lands so the current ps1 keeps working until user migrates to --config.\n\nCross-repo touch: StandaloneMcpServers.ps1 lives in McpsLaunch, NOT in ssh-mcp-kerberos. Do not edit it from this board; documenter will produce a migration guide.','\n', char(10)), 1779761923);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (19, 't_b94988d2', 'orchestrator', 'DEPLOYMENT CONFIRMED: ssh-mcp Windows-host via Task Scheduler (a) + optional Windows service .bat (a+b). HTTP exposure already exists today through mcp-proxy bridge on port 8934 in McpsLaunch/StandaloneMcpServers.ps1; not stdio-only. Added a register-service .bat card and migration-guide tasks. The Option A/B trade-off (keep proxy vs bridge in-process HTTP) is now explicit on R1/P2.', 1779761923);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (20, 't_a60efb40', 'orchestrator', 'Before you start: re-read R1 + P2 results — they will decide Option A (keep mcp-proxy bridge) vs Option B (in-process Streamable HTTP). If A wins, your scope shrinks to (1) wiring [server.http] config metadata so ssh-mcp KNOWS what bridge wraps it, (2) propagating transport/remote_addr placeholders so audit log isn''t blind, (3) leaving stdio internal. If B wins, your full original scope stands. DO NOT pick the path yourself — wait for P2 to land.', 1779761923);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (21, 't_58c0e613', 'orchestrator', 'Reference current production launcher: /home/islaliu/Repositories/McpsLaunch/StandaloneMcpServers.ps1 (started by StandaloneMcpServer.bat). Port 8934, bind $WindowsMcpHost, Hyper-V firewall ''_Mcp Servers Allow Wsl only'' opens WSL subnet 192.168.144.0/24. Two pinned hosts: eip2-db, gitlab (both kerberos). Runbook should compare Option A (proxy) vs B (in-process) flows and tell user which one is active.', 1779761924);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (22, 't_b94988d2', 'orchestrator', 'User decision (2026-05-25): deployment option (b) Windows Service CANCELLED per R1 §8 finding (LocalSystem has no LSA Kerberos ticket; all production hosts are kerberos). Delivering ONLY option (a) Task Scheduler at logon via new card t_e33d1d5e. Old Windows-Service card t_b253463f archived.', 1779762075);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (23, 't_a60efb40', 'planner', replace('P2 planning complete. Plan saved at `.hermes/plans/2026-05-26_P2_http-mcp-transport_windows-kerberos.md`.\n\nDecision: **Option B (in-process Streamable HTTP)**, not Option A (mcp-proxy bridge). Your original full scope stands.\n\nReasoning (short version — full plan has the rest):\n- SDK 1.29 ships StreamableHTTPServerTransport stable inside the ^1.17.5 pin; zero new runtime deps.\n- ssh-mcp must own bearer/origin/rebinding/audit-transport semantics; a proxy bridge hides remote_addr and forces double-process supervision on Windows.\n- Stateful in-process HTTP lets us keep the warm ssh-connection registry across calls — meaningful for Kerberos handshake latency (R1 §3, §7 YELLOW).\n\nKey constraints to honor from the plan:\n1. Default off; stdio unchanged when neither `--transport-mcp=http` nor `[server.http].enabled=true` is set.\n2. Port default 7022 (task wins over R1''s 39998 suggestion).\n3. Bearer + DNS-rebinding (`enableDnsRebindingProtection: true`) + Origin allowlist all on simultaneously — `allowedHosts` is ignored without the flag (R1 §2 verified at node_modules/.../webStandardStreamableHttp.js:109).\n4. Non-loopback bind + empty token = `process.exit(2)` before `listener.listen()`. Loopback + empty token = WARN only if `SSH_MCP_HTTP_ALLOW_ANONYMOUS_LOOPBACK=1`, otherwise also fatal.\n5. Audit writer MUST never receive Authorization headers. Add an assertion to make it loud in tests.\n6. No code change in `src/transports/openssh.ts` other than: (a) conditionally relax `PreferredAuthentications` when fallback creds present, (b) Windows boot-time `klist` self-test (warn-only, mocked in tests).\n7. Windows autostart guidance lives in `docs/deployment-windows.md` stub only — Task Scheduler ONLOGON /IT, NOT a Windows Service (LocalSystem loses LSA Kerberos cache).\n\nRED items called out in plan §9 you must mitigate before merging:\n- Audit secret leakage: extend `sanitizePassword` (src/utils/shell.ts) to strip `Authorization` / `Bearer …` before any audit row writes.\n- Multi-instance race (WSL + Windows host both binding 127.0.0.1:7022): write `runtime.json` lock file with `{pid,bind,port,started_at}` and fail fast on collision.\n\nYELLOW items you can implement with docs:\n- WebUI mirrored-loopback visibility from WSL (acceptable in single-user env).\n- No MIT kinit fallback for the user with file-based ticket caches; document alternate ssh.exe via PATH.\n- Stateful session memory cap (LRU N=64) — pick a number, document, move on.\n\nTest matrix is in plan §8 (T1–T8). T6 uses a mocked `child_process.spawn` for `klist` so Windows AD is not required in CI.\n\nIf the TOML config card t_2d87e8fa hasn''t landed by the time you start, the smallest delta needed is the `[server.http]` block in plan §2 — propose it on that card and add a passing schema test here.\n\nPing back via this thread before the `kanban_block(reason="review-required: ...")` if any constraint in the plan needs renegotiation. Do NOT silently drift from Option B.','\n', char(10)), 1779762082);
