INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (28, 't_a60efb40', 'developer-general', replace('Pre-start blockers found — need orchestrator decision before I can implement:\n\n**B1. Workspace path mismatch.**\n`workspace_kind=worktree`, `workspace_path=/home/islaliu/.hermes/hermes-agent/.worktrees/t_a60efb40`. That directory does not exist, and the path points into the **hermes-agent** repo, not the **ssh-mcp-kerberos** repo where this work belongs. The actual ssh-mcp-kerberos checkouts live at `/home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos[.wt/...]`. Branch `feat/ssh-mcp-http-transport` (from task body) does not yet exist on any ssh-mcp-kerberos clone — only the sibling feature branches `feat/toml-config`, `feat/approval-engine`, `wt/audit-log`, `wt/webui` are checked out as worktrees off `feat/openssh-transport-kerberos`.\n\n**B2. Dependency integration story is undefined.**\nThe plan (§1, §2, §4, §6) requires me to modify and extend code that lives in three sibling feature branches that have NOT merged into a shared integration branch:\n- `feat/toml-config` (t_2d87e8fa) — provides `src/config/toml.ts` I must extend with `[server.http]`.\n- `wt/audit-log` — provides `src/audit/logger.ts` I must extend with `transport`/`remote_addr` fields and the `sanitizePassword` Authorization-redaction RED item.\n- `feat/approval-engine` — A10 requires "approval engine path unchanged" — I need it present to assert.\n\nTask body says **"isolated worktree only; do not touch other worktrees"**. I cannot satisfy that constraint AND meet plan §6 / RED items without an integration base that already carries those three branches. Options I can see:\n\n  (a) Orchestrator (or this card) creates a fresh worktree at `/home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos.wt/http-transport` branched off an **integration branch** that already merges `feat/toml-config + wt/audit-log + feat/approval-engine` into `feat/openssh-transport-kerberos`. I work there.\n  (b) I branch off plain `feat/openssh-transport-kerberos` and stub-in shims for the missing `src/config/toml.ts` schema and `src/audit/logger.ts` extension points. The three feature owners later resolve conflicts on merge. RED #1 (sanitizePassword Authorization redaction) goes into a TODO comment.\n  (c) Park this card with `parents=[t_2d87e8fa, <audit_card>, <approval_card>]` so it only promotes after those land, then I retry.\n\nMy recommendation is (a) — it matches the user''s "complete solutions / one-shot" preference and is the only path that lets me actually verify A10 (approval) and close RED #1 (audit Authorization redaction) inside this run instead of leaving promises.\n\nBlocking on this rather than guessing. Please answer (a/b/c) and, if (a), name the integration branch you want me to base off of (or authorize me to create one as `feat/openssh-transport-kerberos-integration` merging the three).','\n', char(10)), 1779762257);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (29, 't_29114a14', 'reviewer', replace('review: PASS (sibling reviewer t_66e61c98)\012\012Evidence — files read & vitest run against worktree /home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos.wt/audit-log:\012\012Acceptance criteria mapped to code:\0121. Default audit dir = ~/.ssh-mcp — src/audit/store.ts:36-45 resolveAuditDir uses os.homedir()+''/.ssh-mcp''. Windows path: os.homedir() returns %USERPROFILE% on Win32, satisfies %USERPROFILE%\.ssh-mcp. TOML override deferred to toml-config card; documented TODO at src/index.ts:120-122; env override SSH_MCP_AUDIT_DIR honored.\0122. JSONL append per execution — src/audit/store.ts:164-165 (fs.appendFileSync of JSON.stringify(rec)+''\n'').\0123. Size-roll 10MB — src/audit/types.ts:72 DEFAULT_MAX_FILE_BYTES = 10*1024*1024; src/audit/rotator.ts:36-49 rotateIfNeeded. Day-roll via UTC-dated filename src/audit/store.ts:55-57. Retention 10 — types.ts:73 DEFAULT_RETAIN = 10; pruneOldDays at rotator.ts:79-116.\0124. Redactor — src/audit/redactor.ts covers: CLI password/token (lines 26-34), Authorization headers (37-38), env-style assigns (41-42), JSON/TOML KV (45-50), PEM private key blocks (57-58), AWS access-key + secret-hint (61-65), JWT (68), GitHub PAT/Slack/Google API key (71-77).\0125. stdout/stderr cap with truncated flag — capUtf8 at src/audit/store.ts:72-80 (UTF-8 safe), wired in buildRecord at 119-128.\0126. Log write failure non-fatal — src/index.ts:293-296 catches auditErr, console.error, returns silently; SSH result not masked.\0127. Denied executions — types support decision:''deny'' (types.ts:17,23); placeholder yoloApproval used since approval-engine card hasn''t landed (per body, acceptable).\012\012Tests executed (read-only side process, no destructive cmds): `npx vitest --run src/audit/__tests__ test/openssh.unit.test.ts` → 5 files / 28 tests passed (redactor 4, rotator 2, store 4, integration 1, openssh.unit 17). Producer self-report: full `npm test` 86/86 passed against ephemeral lscr.io/linuxserver/openssh-server container.\012\012Security floor:\012- Redactor applied to command, description, reason, stdout, stderr at store.ts:107-128.\012- No secrets touched in test fixtures; uses mkdtemp + stub transport.\012- Legacy sanitizeCommand/exec/sudo-exec preserved (audit wraps post-exec at src/index.ts:398-406, 445-453).\012\012YELLOW caveats (non-blocking):\012- Strict-mode for audit-write failures not implemented — current behavior is always best-effort. Pass criteria allows "unless strict-mode configured"; deferring strict-mode to a later card is consistent with the staged plan.\012- TOML wiring for [server].audit_dir / audit_max_bytes is a TODO at src/index.ts:120; env-var fallback covers operators until toml-config card lands. Documented in handoff.\012\012Verdict: PASS. Orchestrator may complete producer t_67320e65.','\012', char(10)), 1779762323);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (30, 't_67320e65', 'reviewer', replace('review: PASS (sibling reviewer t_66e61c98)\n\nAll 6 audit-log acceptance criteria verified against the worktree. 28/28 audit+openssh vitest cases pass on re-run; producer-reported 86/86 npm test accepted. Redactor covers password/PEM/AWS/JWT/GitHub/Slack/Google + headers + env+JSON+TOML KV shapes. Size-roll 10MB / day-roll / retain 10 implemented. Audit-write failure non-fatal (console.error, SSH result preserved). Denied-path infra present (decision:''deny'' typed); approval wiring properly deferred to approval-engine card with yoloApproval placeholder.\n\nYELLOW (non-blocking, follow-up cards): strict-mode toggle for audit-write failures not implemented; TOML audit_dir/audit_max_bytes wiring is TODO at src/index.ts:120 pending toml-config card (env-var fallback in place).\n\nOrchestrator may mark this card complete.','\n', char(10)), 1779762324);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (31, 't_c857745f', 'reviewer', replace('review: PASS\n\nSibling reviewer t_a2698fcc verdict on approval-engine (commit eb7bd7d):\n- yolo always allow + emits full ApprovalDecision record (yolo.ts:8-16)\n- smart structured {allow,reason}; fail-closed default deny on timeout/non-200/malformed (smart.ts:133-158, defaults to true at smart.ts:84)\n- smart fetch wrapper dependency-injected (types.ts:58-62, used at smart.ts:106)\n- manual: ULID-keyed pending (manual.ts:32-44 — 26-char Crockford), pending/approved/denied/timeout lifecycle, 5-min default (manual.ts:21)\n- manual without WebUI throws ManualApprovalDisabledError at construction (manual.ts:62-65, tested)\n- gate wired BEFORE transport.exec at src/index.ts:299-305 (exec) and :331-336 (sudo-exec); deny throws McpError(InvalidRequest) at gate.ts:51-55; allow returns decision for audit-record attachment\n\nTests re-run by reviewer: vitest run src/approval → 4 files / 35 passed / 0 failed (manual 8, engine 7, gate 5, smart 15). No secret leakage in fail-open warn log (smart.ts:184 logs reason only, not api_key). Tests use vi.fn fetch + fake timers — no live SSH.\n\nOrchestrator may complete this card.','\n', char(10)), 1779762327);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (32, 't_2366a62d', 'reviewer', replace('Sibling reviewer t_a2698fcc audit trace for approval-engine (t_c857745f, commit eb7bd7d):\n\nVERDICT: PASS\n\nEvidence (file:line):\n- yolo.ts:8-16 — YoloApproval.decide returns full ApprovalDecision {decision:''allow'', reason, decided_by:''yolo'', decided_at, mode:''yolo''} → audit decision record emitted as required\n- smart.ts:84 fail_closed defaults to true (this.opts.fail_closed !== false)\n- smart.ts:133-135 non-200 → failClosedDecision(fail_closed, ''HTTP <status>'', ''smart-llm:http-<n>'')\n- smart.ts:123-130 transport/abort error → failClosedDecision with ''timed out'' or message\n- smart.ts:149-158 JSON.parse / missing allow field → failClosedDecision(''malformed LLM JSON'', ''smart-llm:malformed-json'')\n- smart.ts:106, types.ts:58-62 fetchImpl injectable (stubbed in all 15 smart tests via vi.fn)\n- smart.ts:102-104 api_key only added to Authorization header when present; logs (smart.ts:184) print reason only — no key leakage\n- manual.ts:32-44 generateUlid → 26-char Crockford base32 stable id; manual.ts:21 DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS = 5*60*1000\n- manual.ts:62-65 ctor throws ManualApprovalDisabledError when !webuiEnabled → fatal at boot\n- manual.ts:82-90 setTimeout settles with deny reason ''approval timed out'', decided_by ''manual:timeout''\n- manual.ts:100-111 resolve() returns false if entry already settled (timeout/already-resolved no-op)\n- src/index.ts:299-305 — exec handler calls `await gateApproval(...)` BEFORE `t.exec(...)` at :309\n- src/index.ts:331-336 — sudo-exec calls `await gateApproval(...)` BEFORE `t.execElevated(...)` at :345\n- gate.ts:51-55 deny → throws McpError(InvalidRequest, "approval denied (<mode>/<decided_by>): <reason>")\n- gate.ts:41-49 legacy-no-engine path returns synthetic allow → preserves existing behavior\n\nTests (re-run by reviewer in worktree):\n  npx vitest run src/approval → 4 files / 35 tests / 0 failed\n    - manual.test.ts: 8 (boot guard, allow/deny resolve, multi-pending, timeout, late-resolve no-op)\n    - engine.test.ts: 7 (yolo, per-source override, smart/manual unconfigured throws, listPending empty)\n    - gate.test.ts: 5 (synthetic-allow legacy, yolo dispatch, McpError deny, smart-allow passthrough, set/get round-trip)\n    - smart.test.ts: 15 (happy paths, fail-closed for non-200/malformed/no-allow/timeout/transport, fail-open variants, ctor validation)\n\nSecurity floor: PASS — no secret in logs/decision strings/test snapshots; mocks-only tests; legacy behavior preserved.\n\nMinor (informational, not blocking): gate.ts:47 stamps legacy-no-engine synthetic allow with `mode: ''yolo''` — slightly misleading since it isn''t actually yolo mode. decided_by=''legacy:no-engine'' disambiguates so audit reader can distinguish. Worth a one-line comment or a `mode: ''legacy''` enum widening if/when audit-log lands.','\n', char(10)), 1779762328);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (33, 't_b6b0762e', 'reviewer', replace('## Review verdict: PASS-with-caveats (YELLOW)\n\nReviewer: sibling card t_b6b0762e for producer t_4e2a635b (webui-status, commit e76f776, branch wt/webui).\n\n### Evidence captured\n\nFiles reviewed (all under /home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos.wt/webui/src/webui/):\n- server.ts (247 lines) — http server, auth, routing\n- types.ts (110 lines) — interface stubs for queue/audit/registry\n- routes/{profiles,executions,approvals,sse}.ts\n- static/{index.html,app.js,styles.css}\n- __tests__/routes.test.ts (330 lines, 13 tests)\n\nTest run (npx vitest run src/webui/__tests__/routes.test.ts):\n  Test Files  1 passed (1)\n  Tests       13 passed (13)\n  Duration    2.18s\n\nGit stat: 10 files, +1168 lines, single commit e76f776 on top of base 7695120.\n\n### Acceptance criteria check\n\nPASS:\n1. **Off by default / opt-in** — module exports `startWebUI(opts)`; no auto-start on import. Trivially off until wired.\n2. **Default 127.0.0.1** — server.ts:127 `const host = opts.host ?? ''127.0.0.1''`.\n3. **Non-loopback bind requires auth_token, fatal at boot** — server.ts:130-134 synchronous throw before `listen()`. Test `refuses non-loopback bind without auth_token` (routes.test.ts:243) verifies.\n4. **Bearer on /api/*** — server.ts:160 calls checkAuth before route dispatch; checkAuth (line 99-118) accepts `Authorization: Bearer <t>` or `X-Auth-Token` fallback. Test `with auth_token, /api requires Bearer token` (line 255) verifies 401→200.\n5. **?token= for SSE** — server.ts:150 (isSse:true), checkAuth line 106-109 reads query. Test `SSE /events accepts ?token= query` (line 269) verifies 401 without, 200 with.\n6. **Routes match plan**:\n   - GET /api/profiles → handleProfiles (profiles.ts) with approval_mode_effective ✓\n   - GET /api/executions?profile=&limit= → DEFAULT_LIMIT=100, MAX_LIMIT=1000 capped (executions.ts:3-4,19) ✓\n   - GET /api/approvals → handleListApprovals ✓\n   - POST /api/approvals/:id/{allow,deny} → regex on server.ts:184, body.note optional ✓\n   - GET /events SSE → SseHub with 25s heartbeat (sse.ts:47-51) ✓\n7. **Manual approval round-trip integration test** — routes.test.ts:173-204 enqueue → GET shows → POST allow → decisionPromise resolves with `{decision:''allow'', reason:''go for it'', decided_by:/^webui:/}`.\n8. **No credential leakage** — profiles route exposes only name/host/port/user/auth/transport/connected/default — no key material, passphrases, or token values. grep for password|secret|private_key|passphrase|credential found only the test fixture token and the static page token input (type=password, autocomplete=off, never echoed back).\n\n### YELLOW caveats\n\n1. **Spec drift: node:http instead of Express** — plan said "Express + SSE" but developer used node:http. Rationale (avoid ~30 transitive deps for a 4-route server, no rebase churn across audit-log/approval-engine PRs) is sound and ALL functional + security criteria pass. Per pass criteria "confirm node:http implementation passes all security and functional criteria; flag YELLOW if any spec drift" — flagging as expected.\n2. **src/index.ts wiring not included** — TOML `[webui].enabled` gating and `--webui` CLI flag are NOT wired in this PR. The module ships as a library exporting `startWebUI(opts)`; actual boot gating depends on toml-config (t_2d87e8fa) landing. Developer''s handoff comment explicitly defers this ("When wiring into src/index.ts boot, gate behind opts.enabled || cliFlags.webui..."). Acceptable as a card boundary, but orchestrator must ensure a follow-up wires it — otherwise the WebUI is unreachable in production.\n3. **Pre-existing test failures** — test/{smoke,description,persistent-connection,sudo-exec}.test.ts fail due to no live SSH:2222. Confirmed by developer against base 7695120; not regressions from webui changes.\n\n### Verdict\n\nPASS-with-caveats. node:http drift is acceptable per pass criteria. src/index.ts boot-gating is the only material follow-up — orchestrator should spawn a wiring card after toml-config lands. Security floor (no leakage, fail-closed non-loopback, tests use fakes only) is met.','\n', char(10)), 1779762337);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (34, 't_fa50ed7d', 'reviewer', replace('Sibling reviewer t_b6b0762e completed the actual READ-ONLY review of t_4e2a635b (webui-status @ e76f776). Verdict: **PASS-with-caveats (YELLOW)**.\n\nSummary:\n- 13/13 new tests pass (vitest run captured by reviewer).\n- All 8 functional + security acceptance criteria met (default 127.0.0.1, synchronous throw for non-loopback w/o authToken at server.ts:130-134, Bearer on /api/*, ?token= for SSE, manual round-trip integration test at routes.test.ts:173-204, no credential leakage in profiles/static).\n- YELLOW caveats: (1) node:http instead of Express per developer''s rationale — explicitly permitted by pass criteria; (2) src/index.ts boot wiring (TOML/--webui gate) NOT included, deferred to a follow-up card after toml-config (t_2d87e8fa) lands; (3) pre-existing test/{smoke,description,persistent,sudo-exec} failures confirmed by developer not regressions (require live SSH:2222).\n\nFull evidence + file:line citations in t_b6b0762e comment thread. This audit card remains as the governance trace.','\n', char(10)), 1779762338);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (35, 't_4e2a635b', 'reviewer', replace('review: PASS-with-caveats\n\nSibling reviewer t_b6b0762e verified the worktree at e76f776. 13/13 new tests pass, all 8 acceptance criteria met with security floor satisfied. YELLOW caveats:\n1. node:http instead of Express (explicitly permitted by pass criteria as long as security+functional checks pass — they do).\n2. src/index.ts boot wiring (TOML/--webui gate) deferred to a follow-up card after toml-config lands. Module ships as a library only.\n3. Pre-existing test/{smoke,description,persistent,sudo-exec} failures confirmed not regressions (need live SSH:2222).\n\nOrchestrator: safe to complete this card and spawn a wiring card after t_2d87e8fa lands. Full evidence in t_b6b0762e thread; audit trace mirrored to t_fa50ed7d.','\n', char(10)), 1779762339);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (36, 't_50cb0f90', 'reviewer', replace('## Sibling reviewer (t_f8036377) verdict for toml-config (t_2d87e8fa): **PASS-with-caveats**\n\nWorktree reviewed (READ-ONLY): /home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos.wt/toml-config @ 6e0df80 on feat/toml-config.\n\n### Acceptance criteria evidence\n\n1. **Precedence ladder CLI > --config > SSH_MCP_CONFIG > $XDG > ~/.ssh-mcp/config.toml** — PASS.\n   - Implemented in src/config/resolver.ts:37-77 (cliConfigPath → SSH_MCP_CONFIG → discoverConfigPath).\n   - Discovery order in src/config/toml-loader.ts:78-87 (SSH_MCP_CONFIG, XDG, ~/.ssh-mcp).\n   - Unit-tested: src/config/__tests__/resolver.test.ts lines 48-149 covers all 5 rungs of the ladder including the explicit "CLI > TOML" assertion at line 69-87, "--config > SSH_MCP_CONFIG" at 89-107, "XDG before ~/.ssh-mcp" at 122-137.\n\n2. **env:NAME resolution with clear error if env missing** — PASS.\n   - src/config/toml-loader.ts:52-71. Missing/empty env → `Error("Config: <field> references env var <NAME>, but it is not set or empty")`.\n   - Tests at __tests__/toml-loader.test.ts:36-54 including the explicit "never echoes the env value in the error message" assertion (line 45-54).\n\n3. **Legacy --ssh / single-host flags untouched when no TOML present** — PASS.\n   - src/index.ts:225-234 builds cliSourceConfigs from existing parseServerConfigJson / buildLegacyServerConfig paths unchanged.\n   - resolveConfig with `cliSources=[legacy], tomlPath=undefined` returns the legacy config verbatim (resolver.ts:55-66).\n   - Verified pre-existing unit suites still pass: test/maxChars.test.ts, test/openssh.unit.test.ts, test/result-mapper.test.ts, test/zod.compat.test.ts all green (23 tests pass with SSH_MCP_DISABLE_MAIN=1).\n\n4. **No native binary TOML deps** — PASS.\n   - package.json adds `"@iarna/toml": "^2.2.5"`.\n   - node_modules/@iarna/toml/package.json:33 confirms `"dependencies": {}` — pure JS parser, no postinstall, no node-gyp.\n\n5. **Passwords never logged on parse errors** — PASS.\n   - resolveEnvRef error message includes the env var NAME and field label but never the resolved value (toml-loader.ts:66-68).\n   - Improved: the prior `--ssh JSON parse error` log used to include `Raw: ${raw}` (could leak inline JSON credentials); this PR drops it at src/index.ts:62. Net security improvement.\n\n6. **Sample ssh-mcp.toml.example with two [[sources]]** — PASS.\n   - ssh-mcp.toml.example present with two [[sources]] (prod-bastion kerberos default + lab key+sudo).\n   - Test at toml-loader.test.ts:117-138 explicitly asserts "two [[sources]] register identically to two --ssh=<JSON> calls".\n\n### Test execution evidence\n\n```\n$ npx vitest run src/config/__tests__/toml-loader.test.ts src/config/__tests__/resolver.test.ts\nTest Files  2 passed (2)   Tests  38 passed (38)\n\n$ SSH_MCP_DISABLE_MAIN=1 npx vitest run test/maxChars.test.ts test/openssh.unit.test.ts test/result-mapper.test.ts test/zod.compat.test.ts\nTest Files  4 passed (4)   Tests  31 passed (31)\n\n$ SSH_MCP_DISABLE_MAIN=1 npx vitest run  (full)\n29 failures: all in test/{persistent-connection,sudo-exec,smoke.ssh,description}.test.ts\n   → ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:2222 (no SSH testcontainer running).\n   Pre-existing infra dependency, matches dev''s reported reason. Not a regression from this change.\n```\n\n### YELLOW caveats (non-blocking)\n\n1. **ssh-mcp.toml.example uses `[sources.approval]` syntax that doesn''t actually attach.** Line 46-47 of the example shows:\n   ```toml\n   [sources.approval]\n   mode = "yolo"\n   ```\n   The test itself (toml-loader.test.ts:308-311) admits "@iarna/toml flattens `[sources.approval]` as a sibling key" — i.e. this is parsed as a top-level `sources.approval` table, NOT as a per-source override on the preceding [[sources]] entry. To actually wire up per-source approval, users must use the inline-table form `approval = { mode = "yolo" }` inside the source entry. The example is misleading and the corresponding assertion at toml-loader.test.ts:312 (`expect(cfg.perSourceApproval).toBeDefined()`) is a tautology — perSourceApproval is always initialized to `{}` in toml-loader.ts:126. Per-source approval wiring is technically in scope of a future card (approval-engine t_c857745f), so this is documentation-quality, not a correctness blocker for this card. Recommend the docs-examples card (t_310c0ec1) fix the example to use the inline-table form and add a real positive test for per-source approval override.\n\n2. **`audit_max_bytes = 10000` in example** — the example sets the per-record cap, but the plan calls for both a daily+10MB rotation AND a per-record 10000-byte cap. Naming is ambiguous; later audit-log card (t_67320e65) should clarify.\n\n3. **No TOML schema docs in README yet** — expected; docs-examples card handles this.\n\n### Verdict\n**PASS-with-caveats.** All five acceptance criteria for toml-config are met with concrete code+test evidence. Caveats are documentation/example quality and explicitly belong to later cards (docs-examples, approval-engine). Orchestrator may safely accept and unblock t_2d87e8fa.\n\nSibling reviewer card: t_f8036377.','\n', char(10)), 1779762540);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (37, 't_2d87e8fa', 'reviewer', replace('review: PASS-with-caveats (sibling reviewer t_f8036377)\n\nAll five acceptance criteria verified with concrete code+test evidence:\n- Precedence ladder (CLI > --config > SSH_MCP_CONFIG > $XDG > ~/.ssh-mcp): resolver.ts:37-77, resolver.test.ts covers all rungs.\n- env:NAME resolution + redact-safe error: toml-loader.ts:52-71, test "never echoes the env value".\n- Legacy CLI untouched: src/index.ts:225-234 path preserved; pre-existing unit suites green (31 tests pass).\n- No native binary TOML deps: @iarna/toml deps={}, pure JS.\n- Passwords never logged: confirmed; also removed prior `Raw: ${raw}` from --ssh JSON parse error → net security improvement.\n- ssh-mcp.toml.example with two [[sources]] present; test asserts identical registration to --ssh=<JSON>.\n\nTest execution:\n- vitest run config/__tests__/* → 38 passed.\n- vitest run maxChars+openssh.unit+result-mapper+zod.compat → 31 passed.\n- full vitest run → 29 failures, all in persistent-connection / sudo-exec / smoke.ssh / description tests requiring SSH container at 127.0.0.1:2222 (ECONNREFUSED). Pre-existing infra dependency, matches the developer''s blocked-reason; not a regression.\n\nYELLOW (non-blocking, defer to later cards):\n1. ssh-mcp.toml.example uses `[sources.approval]` table-header form (lines 46-47), which @iarna/toml flattens as a sibling key — does NOT attach per-source override as users would expect. Inline-table form `approval = { mode = "yolo" }` is required. Loader test at line 312 is a tautology (perSourceApproval is always `{}`). Fix in docs-examples (t_310c0ec1) and add a real positive per-source override test when approval-engine (t_c857745f) lands.\n2. `audit_max_bytes` in example may be ambiguous re: per-record vs rotation cap — audit-log card to clarify.\n\nOrchestrator may proceed to mark this card complete. Full evidence dropped on audit card t_50cb0f90.','\n', char(10)), 1779762542);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (38, 't_66e61c98', 'orchestrator', 'Critical verification needed: the worktree at /home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos.wt/audit-log shows branch wt/audit-log @ SHA 7695120 (same as base feat/openssh-transport-kerberos) with uncommitted changes M src/index.ts + M tsconfig.json. Developer claimed ''build and npm test passed (86/86)'' but no commits exist on the branch. Possible explanations: (1) dev forgot to commit final state; (2) work is in a different location; (3) tests were run against the uncommitted tree and dev expected reviewer to commit. Please verify: git -C wt/audit-log status, git log --all --oneline, git diff HEAD. If FAIL or work-not-committed, spawn remediation (orchestrator will handle); the audit-log work must be on a real branch tip before the integration merge for DEV_HTTP can pull it in.', 1779762874);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (39, 't_58c0e613', 'orchestrator', 'Port policy update (user authoritative, 2026-05-26): MCPs occupy 8931-8939 (Hyper-V firewall ''_Mcp Servers Allow Wsl only'' already opens this range to WSL subnet). ssh-mcp HTTP transport default port = 8934 (sane reuse of current mcp-proxy port — migration just stops the bridge and starts ssh-mcp directly). Tests may use any free port. Smoke runbook should curl http://$WindowsMcpHost:8934/mcp on production and document a test port (e.g. 8939) for parallel verification.', 1779762944);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (40, 't_80035a6b', 'orchestrator', 'Port policy (user authoritative, 2026-05-26): Migration prefers reusing port 8934 (current mcp-proxy). Phase 3 becomes simpler: (a) stop mcp-proxy in StandaloneMcpServers.ps1, (b) ssh-mcp picks up port 8934 directly via [server.http].port=8934, (c) NO firewall edit needed because 8934 is already inside the allowed 8931-8939 range. Skip the alternative-port branch from the original draft.', 1779762944);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO 'task_comments'('id', 'task_id', 'author', 'body', 'created_at') VALUES (41, 't_4e962fef', 'orchestrator', replace('Worktree update (orchestrator pre-work, 2026-05-26 10:40):\n\nIntegration branch feat/openssh-transport-kerberos-integration in your worktree /home/islaliu/Repositories/ssh-mcp-kerberos.wt/http-transport now contains:\n- feat/toml-config (commit 6e0df80)\n- feat/approval-engine (commit eb7bd7d)\n- merge commit b776e7a\n\naudit-log branch was dirty when orchestrator built integration. AM committed the audit-log work as commit 352287e on wt/audit-log (verified by sibling reviewer t_66e61c98 PASS). YOUR FIRST STEP: in your worktree, run \. Expect a CONFLICT in src/index.ts because toml-config + approval-engine + audit-log all touch the same boot/wiring lines. Resolve the conflict so that all three module wires (config loader, approval engine call, audit hook) coexist; commit the merge. Verify \Unknown command: "test\"\n\n\nDid you mean this?\n  npm test # Test a package\nTo see a list of supported npm commands, run:\n  npm help still passes. After this, proceed with the original HTTP transport scope per body.\n\nIf conflict resolution is non-trivial or requires design intent the plan doesn''t cover, BLOCK with the conflict diff and we will spawn an integration card.','\n', char(10)), 1779763028);
